   "source": [
    "cov = ratings.pivot_table(index=\"segment\", columns=\"method\", values=\"rater_id\", aggfunc=lambda s: \", \".join(sorted(s)))\n",
    "cnt = ratings.groupby([\"segment\", \"method\"]).size().unstack().reindex(columns=[\"gsv\", \"field\"]).fillna(0).astype(int)\n",
    "cov = cnt.join(cov, rsuffix=\"_raters\").rename(columns={\"gsv\": \"gsv_n\", \"field\": \"field_n\"})\n",
    "summary = pd.DataFrame({\n",
    "    \"segments with 2+ raters\": [(cnt.gsv >= 2).sum(), (cnt.field >= 2).sum(), ((cnt.gsv >= 1) & (cnt.field >= 1)).sum()],\n",
    "    \"segments with 1 rater\":   [(cnt.gsv == 1).sum(), (cnt.field == 1).sum(), np.nan],\n",
    "    \"segments with none\":      [(cnt.gsv == 0).sum(), (cnt.field == 0).sum(), np.nan]},\n",
    "    index=[\"Street View\", \"Field\", \"Both methods\"])\n",
    "display(summary)\n",
    "waiting = cov[(cov.gsv_n < 2) | (cov.field_n < 2)]\n",
    "print(f\"{len(waiting)} segments still waiting for a second rating in at least one method:\")\n",
    "display(waiting)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "f22a531d",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 4 · Build pairs\n",
    "A pair is two ratings of the same segment by different raters. When a segment has more than two raters, every pair is used, and the bootstrap resamples segments so those pairs are not treated as independent."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 20,
   "id": "f9f55dd8",
   "metadata": {
    "execution": {
     "iopub.execute_input": "2026-11-20T16:36:06.457042Z",
     "iopub.status.busy": "2026-11-20T16:36:06.456908Z",
     "iopub.status.idle": "2026-11-20T16:36:06.759509Z",
     "shell.execute_reply": "2026-11-20T16:36:06.758403Z"
    }
   },
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "Street View: rater vs rater     161 pairs on 161 segments\n",
      "Field: rater vs rater           153 pairs on 153 segments\n",
      "Field vs Street View            629 pairs on 163 segments\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "def pairs_within(method, how=\"any\"):\n",
    "    rows = []\n",
    "    sub = ratings[ratings.method == method]\n",
    "    for seg, g in sub.groupby(\"segment\"):\n",
    "        recs = g.sort_values([\"visit\", \"rater_id\"]).to_dict(\"records\")\n",
    "        for a, b in itertools.combinations(recs, 2):\n",
    "            if a[\"rater_id\"] == b[\"rater_id\"]: continue\n",
    "            if how == \"same_visit\" and a[\"visit\"] != b[\"visit\"]: continue\n",
    "            if how == \"across_visits\" and a[\"visit\"] == b[\"visit\"]: continue\n",
    "            rows.append((seg, a, b))\n",
    "    return rows\n",
    "\n",
    "def pairs_between():\n",
    "    rows = []\n",
    "    for seg, g in ratings.groupby(\"segment\"):\n",
    "        f = g[g.method == \"field\"].to_dict(\"records\"); s = g[g.method == \"gsv\"].to_dict(\"records\")\n",
    "        rows += [(seg, a, b) for a in f for b in s]\n",
    "    return rows\n",
    "\n",
    "def to_frame(rows):\n",
    "    out = []\n",
    "    for seg, a, b in rows:\n",
    "        r = {\"segment\": seg, \"rater_a\": a[\"rater_id\"], \"rater_b\": b[\"rater_id\"], \"visit_a\": a[\"visit\"], \"visit_b\": b[\"visit\"]}\n",
    "        r.update({f\"a_{it}\": a[it] for it in ALL}); r.update({f\"b_{it}\": b[it] for it in ALL})\n",
    "        out.append(r)\n",
    "    return pd.DataFrame(out)\n",
    "\n",
    "COMPARISONS = {\n",
    "    \"Street View: rater vs rater\": to_frame(pairs_within(\"gsv\")),\n",
    "    \"Field: rater vs rater\": to_frame(pairs_within(\"field\", FIELD_PAIRING)),\n",
    "    \"Field vs Street View\": to_frame(pairs_between()),\n",
    "}\n",
    "for k, p in COMPARISONS.items():\n",
    "    print(f\"{k:30s} {len(p):4d} pairs on {p.segment.nunique() if len(p) else 0} segments\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "4b58590a",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 5 · Agreement statistics\n",
    "\n",
    "- **% agreement**: the share of pairs that gave the same answer.\n",
    "- **Cohen's kappa**: agreement corrected for chance. When almost every segment gets one answer (concrete, no fence), chance agreement is already high, so kappa can sit near 0 even at 95% agreement. This is the *prevalence paradox*.\n",
    "- **Gwet's AC1**: a chance-corrected statistic that is much less affected by prevalence. It is the usual companion to kappa for items like these.\n",
    "- **Weighted kappa** (linear) and **within 1** are for the ordered items: Q6, Q9–11 and Q13. They give partial credit for neighboring answers.\n",
    "- **Strength** uses the Landis & Koch bands on kappa.\n",
    "\n",
    "A pair counts for a sidewalk item only when both raters answered it and neither marked *no sidewalk*."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 21,
   "id": "307b5682",
   "metadata": {
    "execution": {
     "iopub.execute_input": "2026-11-20T16:36:06.761403Z",
     "iopub.status.busy": "2026-11-20T16:36:06.761176Z",
     "iopub.status.idle": "2026-11-20T16:36:13.790273Z",
